{{Term/Store|Restless Cricket|Restless Crickets|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s and [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Restless Cricket}}
Restless Crickets can be found almost anywhere in [[Hyrule]] by cutting [[Grass]] with any [[Sword]] or looking under [[Rock]]s. Unless [[Link]] is [[Stealth|sneaking]] up on them when found, they will hop away two or three times before flying away and disappearing. They are sold by the [[Traveling Merchant]] [[Gartan]] and by [[Beedle]] at [[Dueling Peaks Stable]] and [[Outskirt Stable]]. Using a Restless Cricket in a [[Cooking Pot]] with [[Monster Part]]s will result in an [[Energizing Elixir]], which will grant Link [[Stamina Restoration]] when used.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> They can also be used at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] as an ingredient to make [[Green Dye]].

The [[Side Quest]] "[[A Gift for My Beloved]]" involves Link asking [[Prima]] what she likes on behalf of [[Manny (Breath of the Wild)|Manny]]. She will say crickets as an excuse, claiming that it is her dream to own one hundred of them.<ref name="BotW Prima"/> Upon hearing this information, Manny will ask Link to gather ten Restless Crickets for him while he collects the rest.<ref name="BotW Manny"/> Manny gives Link a [[Silver Rupee]] when the Restless Crickets are delivered.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Restless Cricket}}
Restless Crickets can be found in the Grass on both the [[Surface]] and in the [[Sky]].

